{
  "id": "about-the-author",
  "kind": "epilogue",
  "sourceKind": "about-author",
  "label": "About the Author",
  "title": "ABOUT THE AUTHOR",
  "shortTitle": "ABOUT THE AUTHOR",
  "sourceRange": [
    1226,
    1263
  ],
  "headerSourceParagraphs": {
    "title": 1226
  },
  "elements": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Lalit R. Mishra",
          "bold": true
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1227,
      "role": "section-heading"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "There are people who write books to tell stories."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1228
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "And then there are people who write because silence becomes too structured inside them."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1229
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Lalit R. Mishra belongs to neither category completely."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1230
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "He does not write to explain life."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1231
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "He writes to observe how explanation itself builds a false sense of life."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1232
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "At first glance, his writing may look like philosophy."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1233
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "But underneath, it is something more uncomfortable:"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1234
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "a systematic breakdown of how the mind constructs “reality” moment by moment."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1235
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "His work does not offer motivation."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1236
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "It does not offer comfort."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1237
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "It does not offer conclusions."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1238
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Because according to him, conclusions are where perception stops evolving."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1239
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Instead, his writing moves through layers:"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1240
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "meaning → thought → narration → identity → reaction → dialogue → observation → silence"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1241
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Not as theory…"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1242
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "but as lived internal dissection."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1243
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "He is not presenting himself as a teacher."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1244
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "In fact, his central argument quietly dissolves the need for one:"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1245
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": " if experience is continuously changing, no fixed authority can define it"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1246
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "The tone of his work is intentionally unsettling."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1247
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Not to disturb the reader…"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1248
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "but to expose how much of life is already constructed disturbance masked as normal thinking."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1249
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "He does not ask the reader to believe anything."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1250
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "He only points toward one uncomfortable possibility:"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1251
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": " most of what we call “me” is a process, not a person"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1252
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "And if that feels strange, unclear, or even uncomfortable…"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1253
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "that reaction itself is part of the observation."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1254
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Because in his framework, nothing is outside the system."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1255
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Not thought."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1256
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Not identity."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1257
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Not even the one reading this."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1258
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Lalit R. Mishra does not claim truth."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1259
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "He only removes the urgency to chase it."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1260
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "And what remains after that…"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1261
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "is not an answer."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1262
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Just awareness, without an explanation insisting on itself."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 1263
    }
  ],
  "suppressHeaderNumber": true,
  "index": 23,
  "file": "chapters/23-about-the-author.json"
}
